Draw extent estimate: a negative scissor edge is not "8192 or more" (clang -Wsign-compare).

EstimateMaxY clamps the window scissor bottom and right to int32_t after adding the signed window offset, so they can
be negative, and then compared them with the unsigned xenos::kTexture2DCubeMaxWidthHeight: the comparison was done
in unsigned arithmetic and a negative edge counted as at least 8192. That check only exists to detect Direct3D 9's
8192x8192 "no scissor" case and run the vertex shader on the CPU for unclipped draws
(execute_unclipped_draw_vs_on_cpu without ..._with_scissor). A negative scissor edge already gives max_y 0, so the
CPU pass could not raise it; it only cost a CPU vertex shader run and could move min_y above max_y. The edges are
now compared as signed values, as Xenia intends; non-negative scissors behave exactly as before.

diff --git a/src/graphics/util/draw_extent_estimator.cpp b/src/graphics/util/draw_extent_estimator.cpp
index 4187835..68c315e 100644
--- a/src/graphics/util/draw_extent_estimator.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/util/draw_extent_estimator.cpp
@@ -378,7 +378,7 @@ uint32_t DrawExtentEstimator::EstimateMaxY(bool try_to_estimate_vertex_max_y,
         estimate_vertex_max_y = true;
       } else {
         estimate_vertex_max_y = false;
-        if (scissor_bottom >= xenos::kTexture2DCubeMaxWidthHeight) {
+        if (scissor_bottom >= int32_t(xenos::kTexture2DCubeMaxWidthHeight)) {
           // Handle just the usual special 8192x8192 case in Direct3D 9 - 8192
           // may be a normal render target height (80x8192 is well within the
           // EDRAM size, for instance), no need to process the vertices on the
@@ -388,7 +388,7 @@ uint32_t DrawExtentEstimator::EstimateMaxY(bool try_to_estimate_vertex_max_y,
             scissor_right += pa_sc_window_offset.window_x_offset;
           }
           scissor_right = std::min(scissor_right, int32_t(pa_sc_screen_scissor_br.br_x));
-          if (scissor_right >= xenos::kTexture2DCubeMaxWidthHeight) {
+          if (scissor_right >= int32_t(xenos::kTexture2DCubeMaxWidthHeight)) {
             estimate_vertex_max_y = true;
           }
         }
